From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:21:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/23] rocket: rk3576: vendor first-conv modes for 1- and
 3-channel convolutions

A <= 4 channel layer that was not exactly "3 channels, 32 outputs, 3x3,
stride 2" went through the generic encoder, while its input and weights
were uploaded and packed the first-conv way. The CNA then read far past
both buffers: standalone the job faulted and hung the NPU (YOLOX 001,
MicroNet 000); inside a graph it read the following tensors (MoveNet
Thunder 005, YOLOX).

Route every 1- or 3-channel, square 3/5/7, stride 1/2, non-depthwise conv
through the first-conv encoder with the vendor's mode for that shape
(derived from 3 runtime captures and 31 compiled int8 layers):

 - ic = 3: mode 6 when ow % 16 == 0, else mode 2; ic = 1: mode 2 with
   bit 13 clear (0x20008002);
 - 0x1014 = (sy << 3) | sx, 0x107c = ic - 1, 0x1064 = (1 << ic) - 1 in
   mode 2;
 - CNA output channels padded to 16, weights in groups of 32 outputs;
 - mode 6 width fields for widths that are not a multiple of 16.

int8 first convolutions run as the vendor runtime runs them: the raw
int8 input with the CNA CVT bypassed, and for per-tensor weights the
plain int32 bias mode (0x501c = 0x114). Offset uint8 through the CVT
only worked at aligned widths; YOLOX's 418 wide first conv timed out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
